A||||16||KnightRyder31||Is a 84 Fiero carberated or fuel injected?||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||05-03-2000||03:15 PM||||I've heard my fiero was both carberated and fuel injected.....which is true?<BR>----Knight----||||reg||1
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||05-03-2000||03:20 PM||||Is it a 4 cylinder? Or a 6? The 6s are cross fire and the 4s are carburated to my knowledge. I don't know much about the 4 cylinders though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||05-03-2000||03:26 PM||||84 never had 6cyl. Mine is a four. How can I know for sure? Someone told me it had a TBI Fuel injecter....whatever that means.<BR>----Knight----||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||05-03-2000||03:32 PM||||They are all injected. The 4 has a TBI (throttle body injection) which is bascially a carb looking thing that is the throttle body and the atomizer all in one. The 6 is MPI mutiple port injection which means the throttle body only regulates the air because it has individual injectors and the port for each cylinder||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierospeeder||05-03-2000||05:33 PM||||the older 2.5s were carb<P>but all 84 and up fieros were fuel injected<P>pull your air cleaner off and you will notice a throttle body, there is a large single fuel injector, that sprays onto a butterfly while air is being pulled at the same time, when you press the throttle, you can see the butterfly open up and the mixture divides into the intake manifold to each cylinder.  <P>If you want, you can take the aircleaner off while the car is running, to actually see it spraying which you cant on a v6.  Warning, dont drop anything in there, like an air cleaner nut.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||05-03-2000||10:02 PM||||You know, it takes about HALF as long to actually unscrew the air cleaner cover and look at it than it does to post a message...||||reg||4
Z||000006||Hock||05-04-2000||05:03 AM||||FINNALY! SOMEBODY WITH COMMON SENSE<BR>GOOD JOB SHINER!||||reg||6
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||05-04-2000||09:12 PM||||You know Shiner, I already did that. My friend does not believe me, I told him it was a TBI. He insisted that is was a carberated car, even though I showed him the Fuel Injecter...so dont be a jerk! All I wanted to do is prove him wrong...he thinks he is a genious.<BR>----Knight----<BR>PS. You guys say this is a forum for asking questions...so I didnt expect to be getting picked at!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||TOM||05-04-2000||11:31 PM||||Just because someone can pull the filter and look doesnt always mean they know what they are looking at or for. I took this as they looked but still didnt know. Its an easy mistake to make between a tbi and a carb. They are basicallt the same thing.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shiner||05-04-2000||11:37 PM||||This is not an apology, but it's hard to get the meaning of what ppl say over the net.  I didn't mean it as a "duh, you idiot".  I think a  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> at the end would have made all the difference.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||DJRice||05-05-2000||09:28 AM||||A TBI looks does look like a carb, with the exception of the injector nozzle pointed right down the "Barrell".  <P>Like Tom said, its easy to mistake if you dont know exactly what your looking at (or for).||||reg||1
